---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Story | Aura Homes"
  description="Beautiful second-life rooms that bring people back to nature, one room at a time."
  descriptor="Story"
>
  <main id="top">
    <section class="page-lead">
      <p class="story-kicker">Story</p>
      <h1>One room. Then the land.</h1>
      <p class="story-lede">
        Aura Homes starts with a finished room you can add to land you already have. It sits on a steel frame. The glass is smooth. Everything else on this site is a way of using that room, or a hope we have not built yet.
      </p>
    </section>
    <div class="page-body">
      <h2>The room comes first</h2>
      <p>Beside the house, or out on the property. A door, a long side of glass, and the meadow still in view. The film of that room is on <a href="/">the opening page</a>. The quieter account is on <a href="/rooms">Rooms</a>.</p>
      <h2>Then what the land asks</h2>
      <p>Some sites want a deck, a lit floor, or a few rooms for a small stay. Those are drawn custom, and they live under <a href="/customs">Customs</a>. The order of the later work, including farms and water from the air, is the <a href="/master-plan">master plan</a>.</p>
      <h2>Why it is worth doing</h2>
      <p>The point is a day spent where the light is real. <a href="/back-to-nature">Back to nature</a> is that sentence, said once, without a speech. If you want the notes, they are in the <a href="/journal">journal</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
